            <ArticleTitle>Delirium monitoring and management in the acute care setting.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>37-42</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/01.NPR.0000526764.53348.d1</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Associated with substantial morbidity and mortality, delirium is a syndrome commonly experienced by hospitalized adults. This article presents a case study highlighting how delirium may go unrecognized by the healthcare team and provides 10 suggestions for improving delirium assessment, prevention, and management in the acute care setting.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
